                </div>
                <div class="pi-flywheel">
                    <div class="pi-flywheel-row">
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-role">Vault</div>
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-body"><strong>Your data.</strong> Notes, tags, links. Runs on your machine (or our cloud). Reachable via open REST API and MCP &mdash; so any tool can read and write to it.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-flywheel-row">
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-role">Agent</div>
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-body"><strong>Your intelligence.</strong> Custom knowledge agents you spin up on any vault. Bring the AI you trust (Claude, GPT, local) to the data you own.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-flywheel-row">
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-role">Surface</div>
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-body"><strong>Your interface.</strong> Custom web views to navigate, share, and interact with your data. Notes (the PWA) is one surface; build your own, or use what we ship.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <aside class="pi-notes">
                    <p>The three layers sit on top of a few small modules that ship today &mdash; <strong>vault</strong> (the data), <strong>scribe</strong> (transcription), <strong>notes</strong> (a reference surface), <strong>hub</strong> (the coordinator that ties it together and handles auth), <strong>agent</strong> (an opinionated agent-on-vault distribution).</p>
                    <p>The contract underneath: every vault speaks an <strong>open REST API</strong> for humans and tools, and <strong>MCP</strong> &mdash; the open standard every major lab now supports &mdash; for AI. That's what makes the substrate portable: you don't depend on us to use your data.</p>
