                <aside class="pi-notes">
                    <p>A quick aside on the license: <strong>AGPL</strong> is the license we ship under. It says that if a company incorporates this code into a commercial product, they have to share their own code too &mdash; <em>unless</em> they buy a commercial license from us. Most enterprises won't want to share their internal code, so the license is what makes the enterprise path real revenue rather than a hope.</p>
                    <p>The hosted side is the obvious SaaS line &mdash; most people don't want to run a server, and our cloud is the same modules managed for you. The enterprise side is the patient, higher-margin line that the open-source posture makes possible. Same code in both. Export everything. Leave any time. We're not pricing your context.</p>
